2026-01-07 / 2026-01-08
=============================================================================================

Objective:
Reconstruct individual-level variables from ESS1–ESS8 based on author SPSS syntax and produce a harmonized dataset.

What I did:
Import: kept only variables needed (trust, immigration, authoritarianism, redistribution, economy, controls, interview timing).
Harmonized interview date fields across rounds (ESS1–2 vs ESS3–8 naming).
Harmonized income naming (hinctnt → hinctnta).
Harmonization: restricted to the 22 countries; converted labelled variables to numeric; created interviewdate and applied SPSS-style date fallback within country-round.
Built indices per SPSS logic:
Political trust = mean(trstprl, trstplt, trstprt)
Anti-immigration = SPSS-style non-linear recode of 0–10 items + mean(imbgeco, imueclt, imwbcnt)
Authoritarianism = recode 1–6 → 5–0 + mean(ipfrule, ipstrgv, ipbhprp, imptrad, impsafe)
Redistribution, economy dissatisfaction, and standard controls (age, gender, education, unemployment, income, left-right, turnout)

Main issues + fixes:
Interview-date missing in ESS3–8 due to wrong columns kept → fixed by adding start-date vars and harmonizing.
Type issues with labelled data → handled via label zapping/conversion.
Unemployment coding differences (0/1 vs 1/2) → made recode robust.

Outputs:
data/intermediate/ess_raw_combined.rds
data/intermediate/ess_harmonized.rds

Result:
Dataset builds reproducibly; small interview-date missingness remains in ESS5 (source-data limitation).

