=============================================================================================
2026-02-20
=============================================================================================

What I did:

I re-audited the paper and the author SPSS syntax and found that my earlier ESS import/harmonization missed variables needed for paper-faithful controls 
and DV construction. I updated the ESS import (scripts/02_import_ess.R) to retain the full set of party-vote variables across rounds/countries (prtvt*/prtv*), 
because “one prtvt per country” is not consistently present (e.g., Germany uses prtvde1/prtvde2; Lithuania appears in later rounds with prtvlt* variables). 
I then updated the harmonization (scripts/03_harmonize_ess.R) to match the author SPSS logic more closely after identifying missing demographics/controls in 
the earlier implementation. Next, I implemented cabinet assignment and the far-right-in-government indicator (scripts/04_add_cabinet_and_farrightinpower.R) 
using the author’s government-ID Excel rules by joining on country_id, applying interviewdate cutoffs to select the correct cabinetid, and mapping cabinetid 
to far-right-in-power using the author cabinet classification. Finally, I implemented the far-right vote DV (scripts/05_code_far_right_vote.R) using the author’s 
SPSS party coding logic by parsing the RECODE block from the author SPSS file “ESS1–8 PARTIES NEWEST.sps”, constructing party_key using the author’s SPSS formula 
(essround100000 + cnr100 + party_code derived from party-vote variables), and mapping party_key to partyfam and then to fr_vote (0/1). A key troubleshooting result 
is that Estonia (EE) and Latvia (LV) are not included in the author’s SPSS RECODE table at all; therefore, in a faithful replication, respondents from EE and LV 
necessarily end up with fr_vote = NA rather than 0. This is a limitation/choice in the author-provided materials, not an implementation bug.

Outputs:

data/intermediate/ess_harmonized.rds
data/intermediate/ess_with_dv.rds

Next step:

Generate and record the DV sanity-check table of fr_vote counts by country (including NA counts), and do a quick coverage check for the cabinet assignment and 
far_right_in_power indicator across country-round and interviewdate.
